
{"id":"c1b581ef-145f-4d0b-b15f-31c8ee0ba8b6","object":"chat.completion","created":1785032155,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    capacity = case['capacity']\\n    trials = case['trials']\\n    mem = {}\\n    order = []\\n    for i, t in enumerate(trials):\\n        sig = t['signature']\\n        if sig not in order:\\n            order.append(sig)\\n        if sig not in mem:\\n            if len(mem) >= capacity:\\n                old_sig = min(mem, key=lambda s: mem[s][0])\\n                del mem[old_sig]\\n        mem[sig] = (i, t['reflection'], t['success'])\\n    memory = []\\n    for sig, (lt, ref, suc) in mem.items():\\n        memory.append({'last_trial': lt, 'reflection': ref, 'signature': sig, 'success': suc})\\n    memory.sort(key=lambda x: x['last_trial'], reverse=True)\\n    return {'memory': memory, 'signatures': order}\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to interpret the task: AGENT-RF-01. The output schema requires an object with \"memory\" array and \"signatures\" array. The \"memory\" items each have last_trial, reflection, signature, success. The \"signatures\" is just an array of strings.\n\nWe are given a case payload with \"capacity\" and \"trials\". The trials have signature, reflection, success. The task is to process the trials and produce a memory and signatures.\n\nWhat is the logic? From the name \"AGENT-RF-01\" and the given fields (capacity, trials), likely we need to implement a simple agent that remembers the last few trials that were successful, or something like that? The \"capacity\" suggests a bounded memory of recent trials. But note: The memory items have \"last_trial\" integer, which likely refers to the index of the trial (0-based or 1-based?). The reflection and signature come from the trial, and success is boolean. Also we need to output signatures (an array of all signatures? Or unique? The schema says signatures is an array